        "original_id": "4bb56d23-0562-5bdb-bc13-34f66804e048",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edith Bouvier Beale, Little Edie, Edith Ewing Bouvier, Big Edie, Drew Barrymore, Jessica Lange, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Jacqueline Kennedy, Ken Howard, Phelan Beale, Michael Sucsy\n- Works: Grey Gardens (2009 film)\n- Organizations: HBO\n- Roles: attorney, sportsman\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Phelan Beale was born on May 23, 1881, and died on June 12, 1956.\n- Phelan Beale was an American attorney and sportsman in New York City.\n- Phelan Beale was married to Edith Ewing Bouvier, who was an aunt of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis.\n- Grey Gardens is an HBO film about Edith Bouvier Beale, known as Little Edie, and her mother Edith Ewing Bouvier, known as Big Edie.\n- In Grey Gardens, Drew Barrymore played Little Edie and Jessica Lange played Big Edie.\n- In Grey Gardens, Jeanne Tripplehorn played Jacqueline Kennedy, who was Little Edie’s cousin, and Ken Howard played Phelan Beale, who was Little Edie’s father.\n- Michael Sucsy is best known for creating the HBO film Grey Gardens.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
